# npm 10 silently strips the "libc" platform fields that npm 11 writes into
# package-lock.json. That already landed on main once (952e9fd, 2026-04-03,
# -10 libc entries) and was only undone by accident when later installs
# re-added them. engine-strict turns that silent degradation into a refusal:
# npm 10 now errors instead of quietly rewriting the lockfile.
engine-strict=true
